# Commands

## Framework semantics

CakePHP console Commands (`bin/cake …`) own CLI entry points: arguments/options, IO, exit codes, and batch orchestration. They are not Artisan commands and should not reimplement HTTP controller actions for cron/jobs without a clear shared domain layer.

## Required behavior

- Prefer a Command for scheduled jobs, one-shot ops, and non-HTTP batch work.
- Keep Commands thin orchestrators: parse IO → call Tables/services already used by the app → report results.
- Reuse Table/finder/rules ownership; do not paste persistence logic into Commands.
- Use CakePHP console IO (`$this->io()`), abort/exit codes, and option parsers consistent with neighboring Commands.

## Anti-patterns

- Inventing Artisan / Illuminate console APIs
- Fat commands that hide domain rules and raw SQL
- Calling HTTP controllers from CLI as the default batch pattern

## Review checklist

- [ ] CLI concern lives in `Command`, not a fake HTTP endpoint
- [ ] Persistence goes through Tables; invariants via rules
- [ ] Options/arguments and help text match project Command style
